# --- overnight ACT sweep (2026-08-08) ---
# Checkpoints and logs are large and reproducible from queue.json + results.jsonl.
# results.jsonl IS tracked: it is the record of what was actually run and what it
# produced, which is the part that cannot be regenerated.
sweeps/outputs/
sweeps/logs/
sweeps/results-smoke.jsonl

# These three are SYMLINKS in the kitting-v2 working copy, pointing at the live
# production tree. Git does not treat a symlink as a directory, so the existing
# `outputs/` style rules (trailing slash = directory only) do not match them and
# they would otherwise be committed as symlink blobs pointing outside the repo.
/.venv
/outputs
/recordings
sweeps/*-driver.log

# Sweep checkpoints are artifacts, not source. A 197MB safetensors in an
# unpushed commit blocked pushing main entirely (GitHub 100MB limit) and had
# to be filter-branched out on 2026-08-12. Keep them out of git.
sweeps/**/*.safetensors
.gstack/
jaw_dataset_redbin/

# --- added 2026-09-21, committing five weeks of work in one pass ---
# Grasp-review sheets from the 2026-09-02 corpus audit: 1,900 extracted frames and
# a 400 KB index.html per arm. Dot-prefixed because they were always scratch —
# qa_label.py rebuilds them from the episodes, and the labels they produced live
# in the corpus, not here.
.review-grasps-*/
# Claude Code session bookkeeping.
.claude/
